  "geometryBasis": "The 1910 Berlin cadastral sheet fixes the old street wing corners. The original 1913 dimensioned drawings fix the expanded 94 m street frontage and plan. The Berlin survey aerial independently confirms the whole historic hotel and its garden and daylight courts in 1928.",
  "sectionBasis": "Published street photograph and section drawings establish the horizontal five-storey facade with rusticated base and mansard and hipped roof breaks. The sections fix the scale of upper walls and roofs. The exact published Qualla garden photograph establishes the courtyard window rhythm, terrace and the circular fountain.",
  "limitations": [
    "The reconstruction shows the hotel after its 1911–12 expansion. The conservative date range covers the documented prewar form and ends before wartime damage.",
    "Roof details, exact stone shades, portal relief carving, garden planting and fine courtyard fittings are approximations. The site represents the main connected hotel and its garden, excluding the row of service buildings farther behind the property.",
    "Modern source terrain is independent of the historic building and provides an approximate site datum."
